<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Your questions, answered</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Does Bravo make me visible?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo does not transmit your position. To be seen in ADS-L, you need a Go, alone or paired with your Bravo as a Tango.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does the X1 receive ADS-B with Meshtastic?</summary>
      <p>No. Meshtastic does not receive ADS-B. Bravo needs the skyBlip firmware. Install it by USB-C using the steps above.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>My aircraft has a transponder. Does its own signal show as traffic?</summary>
      <p>No, once you enter your aircraft&rsquo;s ICAO address on Bravo or on the Go paired with it. Bravo then leaves your own transponder out of the traffic it sends.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a Go?</summary>
      <p>No. On its own, Bravo sends traffic to your navigation app. With a Go, you also get ADS-L and FLARM traffic, and the Go broadcasts your position in ADS-L.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a ground station?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo receives ADS-B in the aircraft, wherever the signal reaches it.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
